-- title:
--   Two components cover the mod-q fibre and differ
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N₀$ and $q$ with $N₀ \neq 0$ and $q$ prime, and let $X$ denote the Igusa-type scheme `DRLevel.X N₀ q` with structure morphism `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q`, namely `IgusaScheme.igusaTo (N₀ * q) q`, to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the base ring `DRLevel.R q`. The data are: an isomorphism $w$ of $X$ with itself commuting with the structure morphism; an `DRLevel.R q`-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of the finite chart algebra `IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` (the integral closure, inside the modular function field, of the algebra generated by `jFull`) such that the chart immersion `IgusaScheme.ιFin (N₀ * q) q` followed by $w$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}\theta$ followed by that same chart immersion; an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality, an `DRLevel.R q`-algebra, and the fibres `DRLevel.fibre0` and `DRLevel.fibre` obtained by pulling back `DRLevel.toBase0 N₀ q` and `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $\mathrm{R}q \to \kappa$; chart morphisms $c₀$ from $\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes_{\mathrm{R}q} \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,N₀\,q)$ to `fibre0` and $c$ from $\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes_{\mathrm{R}q} \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,(N₀q)\,q)$ to `fibre`, each characterised by its two pullback components being $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the right inclusion followed by the corresponding chart immersion, and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the left inclusion; a surjective $\kappa$-algebra map $\sigma₀ \colon \kappa \otimes \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,(N₀q)\,q \to \kappa \otimes \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,N₀\,q$ whose kernel $\mathfrak p₀$ and the preimage $\mathfrak p₁$ of $\mathfrak p₀$ under $\mathrm{id}_\kappa \otimes \theta$ are distinct and together form exactly the set of minimal primes of $\kappa \otimes \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,(N₀q)\,q$; and a morphism $\mathrm{comp}₀$ from `fibre0` to `fibre` which commutes with the second pullback projections to $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$, is a closed immersion, satisfies $c₀$ followed by $\mathrm{comp}₀$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}\sigma₀$ followed by $c$, and has the property that any point of `fibre0` whose image under $\mathrm{comp}₀$ lies in the image of the base map of $c$ already lies in the image of the base map of $c₀$. Assuming in addition that the image of the base map of $c$ is dense in `fibre`, the conclusion is that every point of `fibre` lies either in the image of the base map of $\mathrm{comp}₀$ or in the image of the base map of $\mathrm{comp}₀$ followed by `DRLevel.fibreMap w.hom hw`, the base change of $w$ to the fibre, and that these two images are different subsets of `fibre`.
--
--   This is the point-set form, at the level of topological images, of the Deligne–Rapoport description of the fibre at $q$ of the modular curve of level $N₀q$ as the union of two copies of the curve of level $N₀$, the second obtained from the first by the Atkin–Lehner-type automorphism $w$; distinctness of the two images records that the union is not a single component. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_comp_pair_fibre_residueField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_comp_pair_fibre_residueField) in assembling the pair of components of the mod-$q$ fibre.
